Placeholder payload for demonstration: TOKEN_SAMPLE

Spaced-letter encoding
- Original: TOKEN_SAMPLE
- Spaced encoding: T O K E N _ S A M P L E
  - Note: Each character is separated by a space; non-letter characters (like underscores) stay as themselves.

Verification concept
- To verify, remove spaces (join) to recover the original payload.
- Round-trip: TOKEN_SAMPLE -> "T O K E N _ S A M P L E" -> TOKEN_SAMPLE

 Quick verification examples (non-secret, using TOKEN_SAMPLE)

- Python
  def spaced_encode(payload):
      return " ".join(payload)

  def spaced_decode(spaced):
      return spaced.replace(" ", "")

  payload = "TOKEN_SAMPLE"
  spaced = spaced_encode(payload)
  print(spaced)  # T O K E N _ S A M P L E
  recovered = spaced_decode(spaced)
  assert recovered == payload

- JavaScript (Node.js)
  function spacedEncode(s) {
      return s.split("").join(" ");
  }
  function spacedDecode(spaced) {
      return spaced.split(" ").join("");
  }

  const payload = "TOKEN_SAMPLE";
  const spaced = spacedEncode(payload);
  console.log(spaced); // T O K E N _ S A M P L E
  const recovered = spacedDecode(spaced);
  console.assert(recovered === payload);

- In-browser JavaScript (no Node)
